127:   // The number of timeouts that can occur before port migration is triggered for QUIC clients.
128:   // This defaults to ``4``. If set to ``0``, port migration will not occur on path degrading.
129:   // Timeout here refers to QUIC internal path degrading timeout mechanism, such as ``PTO``.
